promote/one_bar_nq_30m/audits/one_bar_dukascopy_2013_2026_20261011.md:21:The runner formed elapsed 30-minute UTC bars from the 1-minute source. Each Chicago session starts at 17:00 America/Chicago. This keeps bars separate through DST changes. The runner retained only bars with 30 distinct source minutes. It used the previous 50 complete bars for each stop level. Native `ml4t.backtest` STOP orders checked the 1-minute OHLC path. The runner canceled the opposite entry after the first fill. It submitted a native MARKET order before the next 30-minute boundary so the next 1-minute event filled it at that opening print. It used a $1,000 protective stop and capped fills at two per Chicago session date.
