promote/one_bar_nq_30m/audits/one_bar_execution_remediation_20261012.md:9:The bounded scenarios used `ml4t.backtest 0.1.7 Engine`. No code in site-packages changed. The installed `StopFillMode.STOP_PRICE` implementation checks the source bar's `open`. It fills at that open when the open crosses a stop. It fills at the trigger when the bar crosses the stop after the open. Synthetic Engine tests verify both long and short entry gaps and protective-stop gaps. They verify that a $1,000 trigger is not a guaranteed maximum loss.
promote/one_bar_nq_30m/audits/one_bar_practical_1m_20261012_mission.md:9:EXACT RULES: Buy STOP highest high of most recent 50 COMPLETED 30m bars, sell STOP lowest low 50 complete bars; both sides valid until one fills; exit by MARKET at next 30m bar OPEN after trigger; $1000 stop-market protective trigger = 50 points for one indicative $20/pt contract; max 2 filled entries per Chicago Globex session date; 30m extended-hours, both directions, ONE contract. No added strategy filters/optimization/regime rule.
promote/one_bar_nq_30m/audits/one_bar_practical_1m_20261012_mission.md:12:- If 1m candle high/low hits both competing entry STOP triggers, do not allow dual fills. Prefer native atomic OCO/contingent execution hook if supported, or minimal well-tested native-engine broker/execution policy adapter. If available create atomic pairing with first-fill cancels other BEFORE fill processing. On unsequenced both-touch minute choose a deterministic pessimistic priority (e.g. analyze both feasible first fills using native hypothetical execution, choose one with worse one-bar return, OR predeclare no entry and separately charge worst loss); do not select favorable side or call ambiguity resolved by OHLC. User accepts conservative model for rare unknowns. Count those events in audit and make them negative-bound sensitivity. If this cannot be integrated with native Engine, proceed with native execution as-modelled, document OCO defect, and make explicit conservative separate sensitivity from native ledger; DO NOT let one edge case block an otherwise useful 13-year proxy MVP. Limit claim to modeled execution, not exact CME.
promote/one_bar_nq_30m/audits/one_bar_practical_1m_20261012_mission.md:15:- STOP_PRICE installed native Broker actually already handles adverse open-through-trigger (verified), prior 3335 artificial 'favorable gap' diagnosis was WRONG. Reuse native order STOP_PRICE and native full-tick costs; don't double charge slippage. Proven actual gap-through fills 286, reconciliation exact.
promote/one_bar_nq_30m/audits/one_bar_practical_1m_20261012_mission.md:21:D conservative ambiguous-fill stress on B: same-minute opposite STOP and same-minute protective ambiguity to worst-case user-approved; where unsupported by native, explicit bounds using ledger, not a fabricated replay.
promote/one_bar_nq_30m/audits/one_bar_execution_remediation_20261012_mission.md:8:1. Previous +$166521.58 cost-aware result used native STOP_PRICE, which grants favorable stop-trigger fills on gap opens: 3335 entry gap cases equivalent to ~$409132.58 of price advantage, and 105 protective stops did not lose additional ~$19993.80 beyond stop on gaps. This dominates net profit. Write exact synthetic stop-entry long/short gap test and stop-loss gap test. Choose native engine stop-market price semantics that fill at worse of OPEN vs trigger on gap, trigger otherwise. Inspect StopFillMode NEXT_BAR_OPEN, CLOSE_PRICE, BAR_EXTREME and fill implementations. Use native supported extension only if needed and legal under repo; no site-packages edits, no manual simulator. Don't claim an additive post-hoc dollar adjustment is a backtest.
promote/one_bar_nq_30m/audits/one_bar_dukascopy_phase567_20261011.md:25:Full-tick PnL is $90,671.64 short and $75,849.94 long. The Chicago RTH proxy bucket contributes $65,686.74 across 2,127 trades; overnight/weekend contributes $100,834.84 across 3,245. These are post-hoc descriptions, not tested filters. Range terciles were formed using the full observed sample and are also post hoc. No confidence intervals were computed because no session-cluster bootstrap was available. No DSR or PBO claim is made because the complete historical trial set is unavailable.
promote/one_bar_nq_30m/audits/one_bar_dukascopy_phase567_20261011_mission.md:12:30-minute bars extended electronic session. While flat, native BUY STOP at highest high of previous 50 COMPLETE bars, SELL STOP at lowest low of previous 50 COMPLETE bars, OCO after first trigger, market exit immediately following 30m bar open, protective $1000 loss trigger per one simulated NQ $20/pt contract, max 2 filled entries per Chicago session day. Use Dukascopy usatechidxusd index/CFD BID price proxy 2013-Jan through 2026-Jul14 and label NOT CME NQ futures, no futures-roll inference. No filters. Preserve chronology, 1m entry/path, delayed stop install ambiguity, off-quarter-tick original price, DST. Existing corrected base run has UTC elapsed bars DST-aware; verify yourself.
promote/one_bar_nq_30m/audits/one_bar_dukascopy_phase567_20261011_mission.md:15:- Reconstruct annual and chronological fixed-block results ONLY from the FINAL corrected cost-aware and zero-cost native Engine trade ledgers and daily equity. Prespecify reporting blocks: 2013-2017, 2018-2020, 2021-2023, 2024-2025, 2026-01-Jul14. Additional per-year results. No model fitting/selection. Highlight the post-2018 and 2026 regime transitions; long-vs-short, Chicago RTH/overnight, volatility regime descriptives as post-hoc attribution only (NOT signal filter). Use trusted ML4T statistics and Polars aggregations for reporting, cluster by session-day for confidence intervals with library bootstrap if available; do not invent confidence intervals, and do not call older observed periods OOS. Compare 2013-2020 vs 2021-2025 structural scaling as index price grew. Report liquidity assumptions and no genuine holdout.
promote/one_bar_nq_30m/audits/one_bar_dukascopy_phase567_20261011_mission.md:22:(3) Investigate and REMOVE the precomputed future data availability gate called entry_valid which uses next two 30m bars: it is future knowledge. A causal native Engine strategy may submit STOPs after current known complete bar and handle actual future missing bars only when they arrive. Preserve exact rule, but report missing-next-open as violation/UNRESOLVED, rather than cheat with future availability. Re-run causal corrected version on dev history. If no way to guarantee next open when data missing, report exact signal/exit exception not silent skip. This is a serious potential source of bias.
