codex
The first audit run exposed an additional clock-arithmetic bug: Polars stores extracted hour and minute fields in small integer types, so `hour * 60` overflowed. That also corrupted the Chicago session-date assignment used to build 30-minute bars. I’ve widened those values before the arithmetic; this changes the corrected feature diagnostics and session labels, while leaving all frozen strategy and trade ledgers untouched.
