Completed the historical corrective audit without rerunning the strategy, accessing holdout data, or committing changes.

**Verified:** Native fills show 44 STOP exits (−$48,058.76) and 194 MARKET exits (+$33,891.80), reconciling to the −$14,166.96 full-tick result. Chicago RTH now uses 08:30–15:00 CT: 61 trades were RTH and 177 overnight. Complete 30-minute features release at the next bar open; the audit found zero release-time violations. The tests also mutate a future one-minute input and confirm earlier ATR and efficiency values do not change.

The report compares the fixed 50-point stop with pre-entry ATR and reports matched-season STOP frequencies by month and by 50/ATR tercile. The 2018 full-year median price is 6,966.5 (71.8 bp per 50 points); the 2026 median is 25,828.5 (19.4 bp). These results support an inference that the stop was relatively tighter in 2026; they do not establish causality. March geopolitical shocks, the April–May rebound, and June technology rotation are labeled as context hypotheses.

